{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5480: implement `cmd/printf` for the go-unix-utils project, covering srd073 requirements R1.1 through R1.4 (Format string and conversion specifiers). This is a stitch task in generation run 44. The task requires creating two files: `cmd/printf/main.go` (printf implementation) and `cmd/printf/printf_test.go` (differential tests against GNU gprintf). The implementation must follow the project's established patterns including SIGPIPE handling, differential testing, and the Go style constitution. Git operations are managed externally by the orchestrator.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **GNU printf reimplementation in Go**: Must match `gprintf` (Homebrew GNU coreutils printf) behavior\n   - **Differential testing pattern**: Using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` to compare Go binary vs reference binary\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main()\n   - **Format string parsing**: Printf-style FORMAT with conversion specifiers and escape sequences\n   - **srd073 R1.1**: FORMAT interpretation as printf-style string, no trailing newline unless \\n in format\n   - **srd073 R1.2**: Integer specifiers: %d, %i, %o, %u, %x, %X\n   - **srd073 R1.3**: Float specifiers: %f, %e, %g, %F, %E, %G\n   - **srd073 R1.4**: String %s, character %c, backslash-interpreted %b\n   - **Non-goals**: No %q, no --help/--version as flags\n   - **LC_ALL=C**: Required for all test environments\n   - **E8 rule**: No function may exceed 40 lines\n   - **E9 rule**: Files under 500 lines\n   - **Build command**: `go build -o bin/printf ./cmd/printf/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd073-printf.yaml** (READ)\n     - Full SRD for printf utility with 4 requirement groups (R1-R4)\n     - R1 (Format string and conversion specifiers) - the focus of this task\n     - R2 (Width, precision, and flags) - not in scope but may be needed partially\n     - R3 (Escape sequences and argument handling) - not in scope but escape sequences needed for basic functionality\n     - R4 (Exit codes and differential testing) - not in scope but exit code behavior implicit\n     - Non-goals: no %q, no --help/--version flags\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/sigpipe.go** (PROVIDED in project_context)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` - must be called at start of main()\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n   \n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (PROVIDED in project_context)\n     - `DiffTest` struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles fields\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` function\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for compiling the cmd package\n     - `NormalizeFunc` type alias\n   \n   - **cmd/printf/main.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Printf implementation covering R1.1-R1.4\n   \n   - **cmd/printf/printf_test.go** (TO CREATE)\n     - Differential tests against gprintf\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full specification before implementation\n   - The task scope is R1.1-R1.4 only, but a functional printf requires some supporting features (escape sequence handling for \\n, basic argument consumption) that are technically in R3\n   - Need to implement enough infrastructure to make the R1 specifiers work while not over-scoping\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task prompt from the cobbler orchestrator containing all project context, execution constitution, go style constitution, task description, constraints, SRD references, design decisions, and acceptance criteria for implementing cmd/printf srd073 R1.1-R1.4.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/printf/main.go` implementing srd073 R1.1-R1.4 (format string interpretation, integer specifiers, float specifiers, string/char/backslash specifiers)\n   - Create `cmd/printf/printf_test.go` with differential tests against gprintf\n   - Run `go build -o bin/printf ./cmd/printf/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/printf/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/printf/ -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd073-printf.yaml`) to understand the full R1 requirements. I was about to plan the implementation approach and write the two source files (`cmd/printf/main.go` and `cmd/printf/printf_test.go`). No code has been written yet. The SRD read revealed that R1.1-R1.4 cover: format string interpretation with no implicit trailing newline (R1.1), integer specifiers %d/%i/%o/%u/%x/%X (R1.2), float specifiers %f/%e/%g and uppercase variants (R1.3), and string %s, char %c, backslash-interpreted %b (R1.4).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/printf/main.go` and `cmd/printf/printf_test.go` implementing srd073 R1.1-R1.4, following the execution constitution's implementation strategy: \"Write all source files before running any build or test commands.\" The implementation must include SIGPIPE handler, format string parsing with escape sequences, all R1 conversion specifiers, and differential tests against gprintf. Per the task description: \"Implement srd073 requirement R1.1 per the SRD specification\" through \"Implement srd073 requirement R1.4 per the SRD specification\" with acceptance criteria requiring compilation, vet, and test passing.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you g