ng` package\n- **Build pattern**: Uses a `testutils` helper (`testutils.BuildBinary()`) to compile the binary before testing\n- **Reference binary comparison**: Compares output against GNU `gecho` (GNU echo) for validation\n- **Test structure**: `TestDiff()` function using `testutils.DiffTest` structs with fields:\n  - `Name`: Test identifier\n  - `Args`: Command-line arguments\n  - `Env`: Environment variables (all tests set `LC_ALL=C`)\n- **Coverage**: 45+ test cases covering:\n  - Basic arguments (single, multiple, empty)\n  - Flag combinations and interactions\n  - All escape sequences\n  - Edge cases (flag ordering, mixed valid/invalid flags, etc.)\n  - Test cases are mapped to specification requirements (e.g., `R1.2`, `R2.1`)\n\n### Key Implementation Patterns for Your Utilities:\n1. **Shared package imports**: Use `pkg/` directory for shared utilities (sys handling, test utilities)\n2. **Signal handling**: Call SIGPIPE handler early\n3. **Manual flag parsing**: Simple loop-based approach for simple utilities\n4. **String building**: Use `strings.Builder` for efficient string concatenation\n5. **Test organization**: Each cmd has `*_test.go` in same directory; comparison testing against reference implementations"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e1e4b87-d3b7-461c-88fd-59cf46415786","uuid":"e6b7354c-ca54-47bc-9c5e-cd5d351490ef","timestamp":"2026-05-22T23:47:34.751Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5480, I need to understand patterns used in existing cmd/ implementations. Find a cmd/ directory that has both main.go and a test file, and show me:\n1. The main.go file contents (pick one that's a simpler utility)\n2. The test file contents\n3. The go.mod file to understand the module path\n\nFocus on finding a utility that already exists and has working code. Try cmd/echo or cmd/yes or cmd/true or cmd/cat - whichever has actual code.","agentI